License for the contents of the data/ directory
================================================

These files are DERIVED DATA: flow features extracted with CICFlowMeter V4.0
from the CIC-IDS2017 and CSE-CIC-IDS2018 packet captures of the Canadian
Institute for Cybersecurity (CIC), University of New Brunswick, including
views produced by the PacAbide transport augmentation.

1. Authors' contributions
-------------------------
To the extent of the authors' own rights (the augmentation transformations,
the selection and organization of the files, and the accompanying
documentation), this directory is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Attribution: cite the PacAbide paper (see data/README.md).

2. Underlying datasets
----------------------
The underlying traffic data remains subject to the terms of the original
providers, which are passed through unchanged:

- CIC-IDS2017 (https://www.unb.ca/cic/datasets/ids-2017.html): made publicly
  available for researchers; any use requires citing
  Sharafaldin, I., Habibi Lashkari, A., Ghorbani, A. A., "Toward Generating a
  New Intrusion Detection Dataset and Intrusion Traffic Characterization,"
  ICISSP 2018.

- CSE-CIC-IDS2018 (https://www.unb.ca/cic/datasets/ids-2018.html): may be
  redistributed, republished, and mirrored in any form, provided any use or
  redistribution includes a citation to the CSE-CIC-IDS2018 dataset and a link
  to the dataset page on AWS: https://registry.opendata.aws/cse-cic-ids2018/

Where these upstream terms conflict with CC BY 4.0, the upstream terms
prevail for the underlying data.
